    narr:generatedFrom "d451297a6dd1dbdf2eecccafc5b2a8b4c1a89a3a" ;
    narr:narration """This narrative argues a sequential four-site migration on the grounds that bounded friction beats concurrent risk. It opens with [a steering-group deadline forcing the cutover shape to be decided](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_1) and [the four sites laid out, one flagged as the one nobody wants to touch](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5). The mainline is [a flat refusal of parallel cutovers, even for the two small ones](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), argued as [contained pain at one desk versus an unbounded double cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13) and [the rota-versus-compound reframing of the desk's objection](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15). The soak begins as [a two-week number defended from a pilot whose exception queue didn't flatten until day nine or ten](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19), then the second meeting adds [the supervisor arithmetic showing a double cutover would pull eight of eleven supervisors off the floor](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11), sharpened into [risk reframed as arithmetic — the constraint that doesn't move](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14), plus [the learning-curve side benefit](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_18) and [a demand that a soak never be shortened because a date slipped](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_28). The third meeting revises the number: [a retraction striking the two-week soak from the plan](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_3), grounded in [the Dockside logs re-analysis showing the queue was measuring a retired weekly reconciliation job](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_5) and [the revised one-week soak proposal](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_9), with [the caveat that the new number is tight, not safe](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_15) and [the recovered time going into the Clyde buffer](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_18), ratified as [the formal note that the two-week soak is superseded](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_20). A position node now holds [the soak-duration basis question with its membership revised](narr:Position_PostGoLiveSoakDurationBasis), alongside [the sequencing-strategy position](narr:Position_SiteCutoverSequencingStrategy). A new advisor pass adds [the advisor's outline of the plan as it stands](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_3), [his endorsement to hold the sequence against pressure](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_4), [precedent from three programmes where big-bang went backwards](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_5), [the warning that pressure to collapse the sequence arrives dressed as efficiency](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_7), and [the directive to write down the reasons now, while calm](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_9). Review acts qualify the arc: [a requested-changes note that containment did not settle the sequencing](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_3), [a rejection asserting no single-site pilot was ever agreed and the call settled on two sites in parallel](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_4), against [an acceptance of the change toward the sequencing-strategy position](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_2).""" ;
